{
	"description": "Golden vectors for screen reading (llm_screen_region / llm_screen_full): the binding parameter, the vision model it resolves to with _shared/modules/llm/vision.json, the request body each API dialect receives, and how a tagged answer is read. Generated from _shared/lua/llm/vision.lua, replayed by it and by windows/modules/llm/vision.ahk.",
	"rule": "parse: \"<backend>\" or \"<backend>|<model>\"; backend matches ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$; model is 1-200 characters, no control character or |, no leading or trailing spacing. A parse vector with valid false is refused; one without model has none. model_vectors: the binding's model, else vision.json default_models[backend], else none (a vector without model). request_vectors compare the decoded JSON body. extract: the text after the first case-insensitive tag, ** removed, trimmed, over every following line; none when absent or empty (a vector without text).",
